/// and VTK’s window centre (2) when the view has them, the shear 0
/// for a single view; a negative <code>far</code> means no
/// clipping range. <code>opacityPoints</code> are the host’s x/y pairs (x in 0…256);
/// <code>opacityTable</code>, when given, is one float an entry of <code>clut</code> instead, the
/// host’s 16-bit CLUT over the value range.
/// <code>crop</code> is minX, minY, minZ, maxX, maxY, maxZ in voxel index units, or empty.
/// <code>shading</code> is on/off, ambient, diffuse, specular and specular power, and
/// optionally the renderer’s lights as <code>VolumeShading</code> sums them.
/// <code>anchoredProjection</code> samples a projection as the host’s VTK ray caster
/// does; composite ignores it. <code>clippingPlanes</code> are four numbers per
/// plane in voxel index coordinates, a·v + d ≥ 0 kept, at most 32.
